<link rel="stylesheet" href="<?=webhome?>style/pishield-device-privacy.css?v=131">
<div class="ps-native-banner"><div class="ps-native-kicker">PISHIELD / DEVICE PRIVACY</div><h2>Device Privacy Monitor</h2><p>See recorded DNS requests for a device. No packet contents or transferred bytes are visible.</p></div>
<div id="psdp" class="psdp">
<div class="psdp-panel"><div class="psdp-tools"><label>Observed client <select id="psdp-clients"><option value="">Choose a client</option></select></label><label>Device IP <input id="psdp-ip" placeholder="IPv4 or IPv6" autocomplete="off"></label><label>History <select id="psdp-window"><option value="900">15 minutes</option><option value="3600" selected>1 hour</option><option value="86400">24 hours</option><option value="604800">7 days</option></select></label><button type="button" class="btn btn-default" id="psdp-load">Load activity</button><label><input type="checkbox" id="psdp-live"> Live (30 s)</label><a class="btn btn-default" href="groups/clients">Manage clients</a></div><p id="psdp-status" role="status">Select the TV's IP or another observed device. If the router forwards DNS, activity may be combined under its IP.</p><p id="psdp-policy"></p></div>
<div id="psdp-metrics" class="psdp-metrics"></div>
<div class="psdp-panel"><h3>Destination categories</h3><p>Classification hints from known domain suffixes and recorded gravity list IDs. Unknown domains remain unclassified. A DNS lookup does not prove a connection or upload.</p><div id="psdp-categories"></div></div>
<div class="psdp-panel"><h3>Top requested domains</h3><div class="psdp-tools"><label>Find <input id="psdp-search" placeholder="Domain or category"></label><label>Result <select id="psdp-filter"><option value="all">All results</option><option value="blocked">Blocked</option><option value="other">Other DNS results</option></select></label><button type="button" class="btn btn-default" id="psdp-export" disabled>Download CSV</button><a class="btn btn-default" href="groups/domains">Manage domain rules</a></div><p>Block/allow creates an exact rule for an explicitly chosen existing group. Check the scope; other members of that group are affected. Rules never replace existing exact rules.</p><div class="psdp-scroll"><table class="table"><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Category hint</th><th>Requests</th><th>Blocked</th><th>Last request</th><th>Rules</th></tr></thead><tbody id="psdp-domains"></tbody></table></div></div>
<div class="psdp-panel"><h3>Recent DNS activity</h3><div class="psdp-scroll"><table class="table"><thead><tr><th>Time</th><th>Domain</th><th>Type</th><th>Result</th><th>Category</th></tr></thead><tbody id="psdp-recent"></tbody></table></div><p id="psdp-note"></p></div>
</div><script defer src="<?=webhome?>scripts/js/pishield-device-privacy.js?v=131"></script>
